| Knight | 24 | 2d6 |
| Queen | 29 | 3d6 |
| King | 37 | 4d6 |

# 10. WIN CONDITION

Dungeon Arcana is fully cooperative. The team wins when The World is defeated. Combat is resolved player-by-player, but the run itself is shared — it isn't over until every player is down. Whoever lands the finishing blow earns bragging rights and the unofficial title of MVP — this has no mechanical effect. Everyone wins or loses together.

**UPDATED v2.3 — **Defeating The World now ends the game entirely.

Once The World falls, the campaign is complete — there is no reshuffle and no next run (see Section 8).

### Optional — The Last Duel (Post-Game)

Once The World is defeated, players may optionally fight each other, player-vs-player, for possession of The World card as a bragging-rights trophy. This has no effect on the completed campaign, and no formal rules are defined for it here — freeform it with whatever's left in hand, or skip it entirely.

# 11. QUICK REFERENCE — SUIT THEMES

| **Suit** | **Theme** | **Combat Role** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Wands | Will, action, drive | Reduce boss ATK |
| Cups | Emotion, healing | Heal own Health Pool |
| Swords | Intellect, precision | Bonus damage |
| Pentacles | Resources, stability | Draw cards |

# 12. DESIGNER'S NOTES / OPEN VARIABLES

As of v2.3, the previously-open variables from v2.0–v2.2 remain resolved into the defaults below. What follows is genuinely optional.

- Combat resolution: each player's own Health Pool absorbs their own failed engagements. No shared-pool mode exists in this ruleset as written; running one is a house rule, not the default.

- Court Card HP/ATK: canon — see Section 9.

- Maze shape: a pre-generated, unbounded directional network, not a fixed grid size. See Section 4.

- Difficulty distribution (default): the pre-game generation described in Section 4 places tiles at random; there is no distance-based weighting in the default ruleset. Groups wanting the dungeon to ramp up with distance from the Entrance can apply the Escalation Variant below.

- Escalation Variant (optional): before shuffling the Dungeon Deck for generation, sort higher-tier Major Arcana toward the bottom of the deck so they're more likely to be placed farther from the Entrance Guardian in the cursor walk.

- Shared Spell Hand (optional): if your group prefers a fully pooled team resource over individual ownership, treat all earned Spells as team property instead of the defeating player's — see Section 7.

# APPENDIX A: PRESET DUNGEONS

For groups who'd rather not generate their own maze, a fixed layout can be used instead: a pre-selected Entrance Guardian plus a set path of tiles at increasing distance from the origin, chosen for a smooth difficulty curve.

- The Novice Crawl — a short, forgiving path for first-time groups.

- The Grinder — a mid-length run with a heavier Court Card density for Spell-farming.

- The Gauntlet — a lean, high-difficulty path front-loading Major Arcana for experienced groups.

*This appendix is a framework, not finished content. Card-by-card layouts for these three presets are planned for a future patch.*

*Dungeon Arcana — v2.3 patched rulebook. Playtest, break it, fix it, repeat.*